1.1.e - UNRELEASED
Fixed - Stutter at the start of every day with large fleets, worst alongside mods whose skills or hullmods check cargo
Fixed - Absynth OP adjustment stripped ships that were never refit on Absynth, including fleets that never drank it
Fixed - Crash when opening a drink or drink hullmod in the Codex from the main menu
Adjusted - The Codex shows drink hullmods with every effect at full strength and links each drink to its hullmod and recipe
Fixed - Sweet Freedom raised market tariffs while drinking instead of lowering them
Fixed - Reapers Blood kept the zero flux speed boost active at any flux level instead of up to 30%
Fixed - On modular ships, drink effects and the Absynth OP adjustment could spread to the same module on every other ship of that type until restart
Fixed - Drink supply and demand stayed on markets after they changed owner, lost Light Industry or the player stopped exporting drinks, and Light Industry ignored the drink inputs it needed
Fixed - Small fleets drank more than the tooltip forecast and ran out earlier than the run out warning said
Fixed - Sweet Freedom lowered the carrier's damage against fighters instead of making its own fighters take less damage, and withdrawal raised it instead of making them take more
Fixed - A blackout could leave you in a pulsar or black hole system, or in a system cut off from hyperspace
Fixed - Crash when blacking out in a starless deep space system or next to a planet or jump point without an orbit
Fixed - Stout kept regenerating armor during withdrawal
Fixed - LunaLib setting changes made after loading a second save in the same session only applied after the next load
Fixed - The fleet left behind after a blackout could rejoin you from another star system
Fixed - The last blackout message never showed
Fixed - Reapers Blood never made ships without officers aggressive, or cautious in withdrawal
Adjusted - The mod folder in the download is now Substance.Abuse, without the version number
Note - Delete the old Substance.Abuse1.1.d folder before installing

